# Packages installed into the image by stages/01-bootstrap.sh.
# Lines starting with # are ignored; there is no inline-comment support
# (01-bootstrap.sh strips whole comment lines only), so every note is on a
# line of its own.
#
# This list is omarchy 4.0.0's install/omarchy-base.packages (basecamp/omarchy
# @ 1c1116b6, 147 entries) plus the Fydetab Duo device set carried over from
# profiles/arch-gnome/packages.list. GNOME is not carried over: Omarchy's own
# desktop (hyprland + quickshell + sddm) replaces it.
#
# Every name below was checked on 2026-08-17 against the ALARM aarch64
# core/extra/alarm/aur databases and repo/fyde/aarch64/fyde.db.
#
# Substituted for aarch64:
#   mise           -> mise-bin       arm64 upstream tarball, built in [fyde]
#   localsend      -> localsend-bin  same
#   quickshell-git -> quickshell     ALARM ships the 0.3.0 release
#   nvim           -> neovim         nvim is only a provides= of neovim
#
# Dropped from the upstream manifest (one word each = why):
#   asdcontrol               unavailable
#   dotnet-runtime           unavailable
#   obs-studio               unavailable
#   obsidian                 unavailable
#   pinta                    unavailable
#   qemu-user-static-binfmt  unavailable
# (all six are absent from ALARM aarch64 and from [fyde]; the first is an
# Apple Studio Display tool, the last a build-host binfmt helper.)
#
# Not carried over from profiles/arch-gnome/packages.list (one word each):
#   gdm, gnome-*, seahorse, geary, vlc         gnome
#   xorg-server, xf86-video-fbdev              x11
#   network-manager-applet, blueman            duplicated
#   nano, lsb-release, openbsd-netcat          superseded
#   bash, gvfs                                 implied
#   fydeos-wallpapers                          branding
#   calamares-settings-fydetab                 installer
# ("duplicated" = Omarchy's shell owns that UI; "superseded" = the Omarchy set
# already ships an equivalent; "implied" = another package pulls it in.)

